<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Elec to sell LCD screens to Compaq.</title>
<headline>LG Elec to sell LCD screens to Compaq.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG Electronics Co, a unit of South Korea's LG Group, said on Wednesday it would begin supplying TFT-LCD screens for notebook computers to Compaq Computer Corp next year.</p>
<p>LG said in a statement that the deal would be worth $100 million in 1997, rising to $1 billion within five years.  </p>
<p>LG will supply Compaq with 12.1-inch TFT-LCD screens.</p>
<p>In addition, LG said it began supplying Compaq with 10.4-inch SVGA screens from October.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
